    <h2 style="margin-top:0">The discount, in plain numbers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Monthly plan:</strong> $150/month instead of $175/month. $0 down. Discount applies for the entire duration of the engagement &mdash; not just the first year. <strong>That is $300/year saved, every year you stay.</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Lump-sum plan:</strong> $3,500 instead of $4,000 for a full custom-coded site, ownership transferred to you on launch.</li>
      <li><strong>Free 5-point audit either way.</strong> If you are not ready to build yet, the <a href="/audit/" class="inline-link">free audit</a> is also free, and I will mark you flagged for the discount the day you do hire me.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who qualifies</h2>
    <p>Anyone with verifiable service in any of the following roles, current or retired, plus their immediate family:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Sworn law enforcement.</strong> Municipal, county, state, federal. Includes corrections officers, parole officers, and sheriff's deputies.</li>
      <li><strong>Firefighters.</strong> Career, volunteer, wildland, and structural. Includes federal/state agency wildland crews and rural fire-protection-district volunteers.</li>
      <li><strong>EMS.</strong> EMTs, paramedics, advanced practice paramedics, flight paramedics, ambulance crew.</li>
      <li><strong>911 telecommunicators.</strong> Public-safety answering point dispatchers and call-takers.</li>
      <li><strong>Search and rescue.</strong> Sworn or volunteer SAR personnel attached to a recognized organization.</li>
      <li><strong>Federal / Canadian equivalents.</strong> RCMP, provincial / territorial police, OPP, S&ucirc;reté du Québec, Canadian fire services, Canadian EMS.</li>
      <li><strong>Spouses, children, parents, and siblings</strong> of any qualifying responder &mdash; same discount, same verification (one shared photo of the responder's documentation, plus a one-line note identifying the relationship).</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>How verification works:</strong> One photo or scan of your department / agency ID, badge with department name, or a recent paystub from a qualifying agency (with dollar amounts redacted is fine). For volunteer roles, a letter from your chief / commander on department letterhead works. Email it once when we start; I delete the file the moment I confirm. I do not retain copies.</p>

    <h2>How to claim it</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Book a 20-minute discovery call.</strong> <a href="/contact/" class="inline-link">Standard contact form</a>. In the message, mention you are claiming the first responders discount.</li>
      <li><strong>On the call, we figure out the build.</strong> Same conversation I have with anyone &mdash; what your business needs, what kind of site fits, which plan makes sense.</li>
      <li><strong>Send proof of service.</strong> One photo of your department ID or a single paystub, by email. Takes 30 seconds.</li>
      <li><strong>I apply the discount on day one.</strong> Your first invoice is at the discounted rate, not the standard rate. There is no "ramp" or "after first year" reset.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Why I do this</h2>
    <p>A meaningful number of first responders run a side or post-retirement service business &mdash; off-duty contracting, security consulting, training services, fire-watch, building inspections, EMS-adjacent businesses. The schedule is unforgiving and the work is harder than the public realizes. If a $25/month or $500 lump-sum gap is the difference between having a real website and not, that is a gap worth closing.</p>

